{"version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"chunk_4ddbb9be4d3ecb72","texts":[{"text":"bash function \"main\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\nPurpose: HTTP/API, file operations\n\n  chmod 600 \"$HEADERS_FILE\"\n  connect || return 1\n  data=$(request_all \"$body\" \"$key\") || return 1\n  case \"$cmd\" in\n    doctor) jq -n --arg t \"$TRANSPORT\" --arg r \"$REPLY\" '{ok:true,initialized:true,ping:true,transport:$t,reply:$r}' ;;\n    describe)\n      local tdata\n      tdata=$(jq -ec --arg t \"$tool\" '.result.tools[] | select(.name==$t)' <<<\"$data\") || {\n        bad \"Tool not found. Available tools: $(jq -r '.result.tools[].name' <<<\"$data\" | head -20 | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\n        return 1\n      }\n      jq -r '.name' <<<\"$tdata\"","tokenCount":156}],"storageText":"bash function \"main\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\nPurpose: HTTP/API, file operations\n\n  chmod 600 \"$HEADERS_FILE\"\n  connect || return 1\n  data=$(request_all \"$body\" \"$key\") || return 1\n  case \"$cmd\" in\n    doctor) jq -n --arg t \"$TRANSPORT\" --arg r \"$REPLY\" '{ok:true,initialized:true,ping:true,transport:$t,reply:$r}' ;;\n    describe)\n      local tdata\n      tdata=$(jq -ec --arg t \"$tool\" '.result.tools[] | select(.name==$t)' <<<\"$data\") || {\n        bad \"Tool not found. Available tools: $(jq -r '.result.tools[].name' <<<\"$data\" | head -20 | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\n        return 1\n      }\n      jq -r '.name' <<<\"$tdata\"","content":"  chmod 600 \"$HEADERS_FILE\"\n  connect || return 1\n  data=$(request_all \"$body\" \"$key\") || return 1\n  case \"$cmd\" in\n    doctor) jq -n --arg t \"$TRANSPORT\" --arg r \"$REPLY\" '{ok:true,initialized:true,ping:true,transport:$t,reply:$r}' ;;\n    describe)\n      local tdata\n      tdata=$(jq -ec --arg t \"$tool\" '.result.tools[] | select(.name==$t)' <<<\"$data\") || {\n        bad \"Tool not found. Available tools: $(jq -r '.result.tools[].name' <<<\"$data\" | head -20 | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\n        return 1\n      }\n      jq -r '.name' <<<\"$tdata\"","contentHash":"f5771f3b951d25ad","metadata":{"filePath":"skills/figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh","startLine":476,"endLine":487,"chunkType":"function_definition","name":"main","language":"bash","hash":"f5771f3b951d25ad"}}],"error":"Google embedding provider returned HTTP 400.","attemptCount":10,"lastAttempt":"2026-10-17T11:40:23.914Z"}
{"version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"chunk_836f4d2c7261ad49","texts":[{"text":"bash function \"main\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\nPurpose: data parsing\n\n        return 1\n      }\n      jq -r '.name' <<<\"$tdata\"\n      jq -r '.description // empty' <<<\"$tdata\"\n      echo 'arguments:'\n      local props\n      props=$(jq -c '.inputSchema.properties // {}' <<<\"$tdata\")\n      if [ \"$(jq 'length' <<<\"$props\")\" -eq 0 ]; then echo '  (none)'; else\n        jq -r --argjson req \"$(jq -c '.inputSchema.required // []' <<<\"$tdata\")\" '\n          def tstr: if type == \"array\" then (map(tostring)|join(\"|\")) else tostring end;\n          to_entries[] |\n          \"  \" + .key + \" (\" + ((.value.type // \"any\") | tstr) + (if (.key as $k | $req | index($k)) then \", required\" else \"\" end) + \") — \" + (.value.description // \"\")","tokenCount":184}],"storageText":"bash function \"main\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\nPurpose: data parsing\n\n        return 1\n      }\n      jq -r '.name' <<<\"$tdata\"\n      jq -r '.description // empty' <<<\"$tdata\"\n      echo 'arguments:'\n      local props\n      props=$(jq -c '.inputSchema.properties // {}' <<<\"$tdata\")\n      if [ \"$(jq 'length' <<<\"$props\")\" -eq 0 ]; then echo '  (none)'; else\n        jq -r --argjson req \"$(jq -c '.inputSchema.required // []' <<<\"$tdata\")\" '\n          def tstr: if type == \"array\" then (map(tostring)|join(\"|\")) else tostring end;\n          to_entries[] |\n          \"  \" + .key + \" (\" + ((.value.type // \"any\") | tstr) + (if (.key as $k | $req | index($k)) then \", required\" else \"\" end) + \") — \" + (.value.description // \"\")","content":"        return 1\n      }\n      jq -r '.name' <<<\"$tdata\"\n      jq -r '.description // empty' <<<\"$tdata\"\n      echo 'arguments:'\n      local props\n      props=$(jq -c '.inputSchema.properties // {}' <<<\"$tdata\")\n      if [ \"$(jq 'length' <<<\"$props\")\" -eq 0 ]; then echo '  (none)'; else\n        jq -r --argjson req \"$(jq -c '.inputSchema.required // []' <<<\"$tdata\")\" '\n          def tstr: if type == \"array\" then (map(tostring)|join(\"|\")) else tostring end;\n          to_entries[] |\n          \"  \" + .key + \" (\" + ((.value.type // \"any\") | tstr) + (if (.key as $k | $req | index($k)) then \", required\" else \"\" end) + \") — \" + (.value.description // \"\")","contentHash":"2225394509c19a40","metadata":{"filePath":"skills/figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh","startLine":485,"endLine":496,"chunkType":"function_definition","name":"main","language":"bash","hash":"2225394509c19a40"}}],"error":"Google embedding provider returned HTTP 400.","attemptCount":10,"lastAttempt":"2026-10-17T11:40:23.914Z"}
{"version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"chunk_4e8691373ebbc930","texts":[{"text":"bash function \"main\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\nPurpose: placeholder(), data parsing\n\n          def tstr: if type == \"array\" then (map(tostring)|join(\"|\")) else tostring end;\n          to_entries[] |\n          \"  \" + .key + \" (\" + ((.value.type // \"any\") | tstr) + (if (.key as $k | $req | index($k)) then \", required\" else \"\" end) + \") — \" + (.value.description // \"\")\n        ' <<<\"$props\"\n      fi\n      echo 'example:'\n      jq -c --argjson req \"$(jq -c '.inputSchema.required // []' <<<\"$tdata\")\" --argjson props \"$props\" '\n        def placeholder($t):\n          if $t == \"string\" then \"...\"\n          elif ($t == \"number\" or $t == \"integer\") then 0\n          elif $t == \"boolean\" then false\n          elif $t == \"array\" then []","tokenCount":186}],"storageText":"bash function \"main\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\nPurpose: placeholder(), data parsing\n\n          def tstr: if type == \"array\" then (map(tostring)|join(\"|\")) else tostring end;\n          to_entries[] |\n          \"  \" + .key + \" (\" + ((.value.type // \"any\") | tstr) + (if (.key as $k | $req | index($k)) then \", required\" else \"\" end) + \") — \" + (.value.description // \"\")\n        ' <<<\"$props\"\n      fi\n      echo 'example:'\n      jq -c --argjson req \"$(jq -c '.inputSchema.required // []' <<<\"$tdata\")\" --argjson props \"$props\" '\n        def placeholder($t):\n          if $t == \"string\" then \"...\"\n          elif ($t == \"number\" or $t == \"integer\") then 0\n          elif $t == \"boolean\" then false\n          elif $t == \"array\" then []","content":"          def tstr: if type == \"array\" then (map(tostring)|join(\"|\")) else tostring end;\n          to_entries[] |\n          \"  \" + .key + \" (\" + ((.value.type // \"any\") | tstr) + (if (.key as $k | $req | index($k)) then \", required\" else \"\" end) + \") — \" + (.value.description // \"\")\n        ' <<<\"$props\"\n      fi\n      echo 'example:'\n      jq -c --argjson req \"$(jq -c '.inputSchema.required // []' <<<\"$tdata\")\" --argjson props \"$props\" '\n        def placeholder($t):\n          if $t == \"string\" then \"...\"\n          elif ($t == \"number\" or $t == \"integer\") then 0\n          elif $t == \"boolean\" then false\n          elif $t == \"array\" then []","contentHash":"f47ed4195478464d","metadata":{"filePath":"skills/figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh","startLine":494,"endLine":505,"chunkType":"function_definition","name":"main","language":"bash","hash":"f47ed4195478464d"}}],"error":"Google embedding provider returned HTTP 400.","attemptCount":10,"lastAttempt":"2026-10-17T11:40:23.914Z"}
{"version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"chunk_cdaf09030e1fe512","texts":[{"text":"bash function \"http_post\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\nPurpose: authentication, token management, user management, authorization, validation, error handling\n\nhttp_post() {\n  local body=\"$1\" status\n  status=$(curl -q -sS --proto '=http,https' --max-time \"$TIMEOUT\" -D \"$WORK/headers\" -o \"$WORK/body\" \\\n    -w '%{http_code}' -X POST \"$URL\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n    -H 'Accept: application/json, text/event-stream' -H @\"$HEADERS_FILE\" \\\n    \"${SESSION_HEADERS[@]+\"${SESSION_HEADERS[@]}\"}\" --data-binary \"$body\" 2>\"$WORK/curlerr\") || {\n      bad \"Connection failed or timed out. Check the server and retry with --timeout 90.\"; return 1;\n    }\n  # curl failure (empty status)\n  if [ -z \"$status\" ]; then\n    local cerr\n    cerr=$(cat \"$WORK/curlerr\" 2>/dev/null)\n    bad \"Connection failed or timed out. $cerr Check the server and retry with --timeout 90.\"\n    return 1\n  fi\n  case \"$status\" in\n    2??) \n      # detect non-MCP html\n      if grep -qi '^content-type:.*text/html' \"$WORK/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n        bad \"HTTP $status: not a streamable-HTTP MCP endpoint (text/html). Check the URL path.\"\n        return 1\n      fi\n      return 0 ;;\n    401) bad \"HTTP 401: authorization failed. Pass a token via --header 'Authorization: Bearer ...' or a named server with \\${ENV_VAR}.\" ;;\n    403) bad \"HTTP 403: forbidden. Check account permissions.\" ;;\n    404) bad \"HTTP 404: endpoint or session unavailable. Check the URL path or start a new session.\" ;;\n    405|406) bad \"HTTP $status: method or content type not allowed. Check the endpoint.\" ;;\n    429) bad \"HTTP 429: rate limited. Retry later.\" ;;\n    5*) bad \"HTTP $status: server error. Check server health.\" ;;\n    *) bad \"HTTP $status: request failed.\" ;;\n  esac\n  # try show JSON-RPC error message\n  if [ -s \"$WORK/body\" ]; then\n    local msg\n    msg=$(jq -r '.error.message // empty' \"$WORK/body\" 2>/dev/null)\n    [ -z \"$msg\" ] || bad \"Server said: $msg\"\n  fi\n  return 1\n}","tokenCount":490}],"storageText":"bash function \"http_post\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\nPurpose: authentication, token management, user management, authorization, validation, error handling\n\nhttp_post() {\n  local body=\"$1\" status\n  status=$(curl -q -sS --proto '=http,https' --max-time \"$TIMEOUT\" -D \"$WORK/headers\" -o \"$WORK/body\" \\\n    -w '%{http_code}' -X POST \"$URL\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n    -H 'Accept: application/json, text/event-stream' -H @\"$HEADERS_FILE\" \\\n    \"${SESSION_HEADERS[@]+\"${SESSION_HEADERS[@]}\"}\" --data-binary \"$body\" 2>\"$WORK/curlerr\") || {\n      bad \"Connection failed or timed out. Check the server and retry with --timeout 90.\"; return 1;\n    }\n  # curl failure (empty status)\n  if [ -z \"$status\" ]; then\n    local cerr\n    cerr=$(cat \"$WORK/curlerr\" 2>/dev/null)\n    bad \"Connection failed or timed out. $cerr Check the server and retry with --timeout 90.\"\n    return 1\n  fi\n  case \"$status\" in\n    2??) \n      # detect non-MCP html\n      if grep -qi '^content-type:.*text/html' \"$WORK/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n        bad \"HTTP $status: not a streamable-HTTP MCP endpoint (text/html). Check the URL path.\"\n        return 1\n      fi\n      return 0 ;;\n    401) bad \"HTTP 401: authorization failed. Pass a token via --header 'Authorization: Bearer ...' or a named server with \\${ENV_VAR}.\" ;;\n    403) bad \"HTTP 403: forbidden. Check account permissions.\" ;;\n    404) bad \"HTTP 404: endpoint or session unavailable. Check the URL path or start a new session.\" ;;\n    405|406) bad \"HTTP $status: method or content type not allowed. Check the endpoint.\" ;;\n    429) bad \"HTTP 429: rate limited. Retry later.\" ;;\n    5*) bad \"HTTP $status: server error. Check server health.\" ;;\n    *) bad \"HTTP $status: request failed.\" ;;\n  esac\n  # try show JSON-RPC error message\n  if [ -s \"$WORK/body\" ]; then\n    local msg\n    msg=$(jq -r '.error.message // empty' \"$WORK/body\" 2>/dev/null)\n    [ -z \"$msg\" ] || bad \"Server said: $msg\"\n  fi\n  return 1\n}","content":"http_post() {\n  local body=\"$1\" status\n  status=$(curl -q -sS --proto '=http,https' --max-time \"$TIMEOUT\" -D \"$WORK/headers\" -o \"$WORK/body\" \\\n    -w '%{http_code}' -X POST \"$URL\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n    -H 'Accept: application/json, text/event-stream' -H @\"$HEADERS_FILE\" \\\n    \"${SESSION_HEADERS[@]+\"${SESSION_HEADERS[@]}\"}\" --data-binary \"$body\" 2>\"$WORK/curlerr\") || {\n      bad \"Connection failed or timed out. Check the server and retry with --timeout 90.\"; return 1;\n    }\n  # curl failure (empty status)\n  if [ -z \"$status\" ]; then\n    local cerr\n    cerr=$(cat \"$WORK/curlerr\" 2>/dev/null)\n    bad \"Connection failed or timed out. $cerr Check the server and retry with --timeout 90.\"\n    return 1\n  fi\n  case \"$status\" in\n    2??) \n      # detect non-MCP html\n      if grep -qi '^content-type:.*text/html' \"$WORK/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n        bad \"HTTP $status: not a streamable-HTTP MCP endpoint (text/html). Check the URL path.\"\n        return 1\n      fi\n      return 0 ;;\n    401) bad \"HTTP 401: authorization failed. Pass a token via --header 'Authorization: Bearer ...' or a named server with \\${ENV_VAR}.\" ;;\n    403) bad \"HTTP 403: forbidden. Check account permissions.\" ;;\n    404) bad \"HTTP 404: endpoint or session unavailable. Check the URL path or start a new session.\" ;;\n    405|406) bad \"HTTP $status: method or content type not allowed. Check the endpoint.\" ;;\n    429) bad \"HTTP 429: rate limited. Retry later.\" ;;\n    5*) bad \"HTTP $status: server error. Check server health.\" ;;\n    *) bad \"HTTP $status: request failed.\" ;;\n  esac\n  # try show JSON-RPC error message\n  if [ -s \"$WORK/body\" ]; then\n    local msg\n    msg=$(jq -r '.error.message // empty' \"$WORK/body\" 2>/dev/null)\n    [ -z \"$msg\" ] || bad \"Server said: $msg\"\n  fi\n  return 1\n}","contentHash":"b3f699c56199379b","metadata":{"filePath":"skills/figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh","startLine":88,"endLine":126,"chunkType":"function_definition","name":"http_post","language":"bash","hash":"b3f699c56199379b"}}],"error":"Google embedding provider returned HTTP 400.","attemptCount":10,"lastAttempt":"2026-10-17T11:40:23.914Z"}
{"version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"chunk_2f4b610c63f3ecc5","texts":[{"text":"bash function \"stdio_send\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\n\nstdio_send() { printf '%s\\n' \"$1\" >&3; }","tokenCount":26}],"storageText":"bash function \"stdio_send\"\nin figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh\n\nstdio_send() { printf '%s\\n' \"$1\" >&3; }","content":"stdio_send() { printf '%s\\n' \"$1\" >&3; }","contentHash":"3113aa9514d71bf0","metadata":{"filePath":"skills/figma-verify/scripts/mcp-wire.sh","startLine":128,"endLine":128,"chunkType":"function_definition","name":"stdio_send","language":"bash","hash":"3113aa9514d71bf0"}}],"error":"Google embedding provider returned HTTP 400.","attemptCount":10,"lastAttempt":"2026-10-17T11:40:23.914Z"}
{"version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"chunk_5482f21672632516","texts":[{"text":"markdown block\nin docs/research/2026-09-29-user-needs.md\nPurpose: authentication, token management, logging, HTTP/API, file operations, encryption/cryptography\n\npaginated servers today — same bug class as mcp-cli#206.\n\n### 8. Long-running tools: streaming/progress, async tasks, cancellation\n**How often:** smaller but growing with the 2026-07-28 spec (tasks).\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [typescript-sdk#245 — client times out after 60s ignoring timeout option](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/issues/245) (17 reactions)\n- [mcp-remote#226 — SSE transport hangs indefinitely on long-running requests](https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/issues/226)\n- apify/mcpc#168/#169/#181 — `tasks-result`, Ctrl+C task hints, async polling UX\n\n**Difficulty:** hard in bash (incremental SSE consumption, keep-alive, task\npolling loops). Defer; `--timeout` already covers the basic case.\n\n### 9. Config file / named servers\n**How often:** open spec ask + competitor configs.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [modelcontextprotocol#292 — Define a Standard MCP Configuration Schema](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/292) (50 reactions, open)\n- [philschmid/mcp-cli#260 — {file:path} substitution for secrets](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/260), [#217 — info command leaks secrets](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/217), [#28 — merge of MCP configuration files](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/28)\n- mcpx `mcpx add <name> --url <url>` pattern\n\n**Difficulty:** easy — a sourceable `~/.config/mcp-wire/config` mapping\nname → url + headers (`mcp-wire figma list`). Already flagged on the map\n(#5) as hanging on engine-scope.\n\n### 10. Platform coverage (Windows/WSL, arm64)\n**How often:** mcp-remote 'windows' 28 issues; mcp-cli#24 (Linux arm64).\n\n**Strongest evidence:** [mcp-remote#316 — Windows OAuth callback listener failure](https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/issues/316), [mcp-cli#24 — Not working on Linux arm64](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/24)\n","tokenCount":511}],"storageText":"markdown block\nin docs/research/2026-09-29-user-needs.md\nPurpose: authentication, token management, logging, HTTP/API, file operations, encryption/cryptography\n\npaginated servers today — same bug class as mcp-cli#206.\n\n### 8. Long-running tools: streaming/progress, async tasks, cancellation\n**How often:** smaller but growing with the 2026-07-28 spec (tasks).\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [typescript-sdk#245 — client times out after 60s ignoring timeout option](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/issues/245) (17 reactions)\n- [mcp-remote#226 — SSE transport hangs indefinitely on long-running requests](https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/issues/226)\n- apify/mcpc#168/#169/#181 — `tasks-result`, Ctrl+C task hints, async polling UX\n\n**Difficulty:** hard in bash (incremental SSE consumption, keep-alive, task\npolling loops). Defer; `--timeout` already covers the basic case.\n\n### 9. Config file / named servers\n**How often:** open spec ask + competitor configs.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [modelcontextprotocol#292 — Define a Standard MCP Configuration Schema](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/292) (50 reactions, open)\n- [philschmid/mcp-cli#260 — {file:path} substitution for secrets](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/260), [#217 — info command leaks secrets](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/217), [#28 — merge of MCP configuration files](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/28)\n- mcpx `mcpx add <name> --url <url>` pattern\n\n**Difficulty:** easy — a sourceable `~/.config/mcp-wire/config` mapping\nname → url + headers (`mcp-wire figma list`). Already flagged on the map\n(#5) as hanging on engine-scope.\n\n### 10. Platform coverage (Windows/WSL, arm64)\n**How often:** mcp-remote 'windows' 28 issues; mcp-cli#24 (Linux arm64).\n\n**Strongest evidence:** [mcp-remote#316 — Windows OAuth callback listener failure](https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/issues/316), [mcp-cli#24 — Not working on Linux arm64](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/24)\n","content":"paginated servers today — same bug class as mcp-cli#206.\n\n### 8. Long-running tools: streaming/progress, async tasks, cancellation\n**How often:** smaller but growing with the 2026-07-28 spec (tasks).\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [typescript-sdk#245 — client times out after 60s ignoring timeout option](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/issues/245) (17 reactions)\n- [mcp-remote#226 — SSE transport hangs indefinitely on long-running requests](https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/issues/226)\n- apify/mcpc#168/#169/#181 — `tasks-result`, Ctrl+C task hints, async polling UX\n\n**Difficulty:** hard in bash (incremental SSE consumption, keep-alive, task\npolling loops). Defer; `--timeout` already covers the basic case.\n\n### 9. Config file / named servers\n**How often:** open spec ask + competitor configs.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [modelcontextprotocol#292 — Define a Standard MCP Configuration Schema](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/292) (50 reactions, open)\n- [philschmid/mcp-cli#260 — {file:path} substitution for secrets](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/260), [#217 — info command leaks secrets](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/217), [#28 — merge of MCP configuration files](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/28)\n- mcpx `mcpx add <name> --url <url>` pattern\n\n**Difficulty:** easy — a sourceable `~/.config/mcp-wire/config` mapping\nname → url + headers (`mcp-wire figma list`). Already flagged on the map\n(#5) as hanging on engine-scope.\n\n### 10. Platform coverage (Windows/WSL, arm64)\n**How often:** mcp-remote 'windows' 28 issues; mcp-cli#24 (Linux arm64).\n\n**Strongest evidence:** [mcp-remote#316 — Windows OAuth callback listener failure](https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/issues/316), [mcp-cli#24 — Not working on Linux arm64](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/24)\n","contentHash":"928540cb2245feb4","metadata":{"filePath":"docs/research/2026-09-29-user-needs.md","startLine":136,"endLine":165,"chunkType":"block","language":"markdown","hash":"928540cb2245feb4"}}],"error":"Google embedding provider returned HTTP 400.","attemptCount":11,"lastAttempt":"2026-10-17T11:40:23.914Z"}
{"version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"chunk_e300f26ed210e99b","texts":[{"text":"markdown block\nin docs/research/2026-09-29-user-needs.md\nPurpose: authentication, token management, logging, caching, HTTP/API, file operations\n\n\n**Strongest evidence:** [mcp-remote#316 — Windows OAuth callback listener failure](https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/issues/316), [mcp-cli#24 — Not working on Linux arm64](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/24)\n\n**Difficulty:** for mcp-wire: docs-only (document WSL; jq/curl exist on arm64).\nNative Windows bash port is out of scope per the family's \"bash + npm + GitHub\"\nboundary.\n\n---\n\n## Bucket 2 — DISTRIBUTION / PACKAGING (ranked)\n\n### 1. Zero-runtime, one-line install — \"no node\" is a feature\n**How often:** the most-reacted distribution complaint in the whole MCP space.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [modelcontextprotocol/servers#64 — MCP Servers Don't Work with NVM](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/issues/64) (182 reactions) — node-version hell is the #1 pain of the npx-stdio ecosystem\n- [inspector#326 — `mcp-inspector: command not found` after upgrade](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/issues/326) (20) and [#873 — phantom dependencies](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/issues/873) (12)\n- Distribution evidence: [turlockmike/murl](https://github.com/turlockmike/murl) ships a Homebrew tap; mcpx ships binary + npm + curl script; [evantahler post](https://www.evantahler.com/blog/post/2026-03-13-curl-for-mcp) — \"agents already know curl, git, docker, npm\"\n\n**Difficulty:** low. mcp-wire already has the two winning artifacts (single-file\ncurl install; npm two-tier package). Add a Homebrew tap + keep the engine\ndependency-free (bash/curl/jq only). This is the moat vs. node-based mcpc.\n\n### 2. Agent-harness / skills-ecosystem compatibility\n**How often:** vercel-labs/skills issue tracker is dominated by it — install\npaths, symlinks, lockfiles, versioning.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [vercel-labs/skills#744 — `npx skills add` doesn't create symlinks in ~/.claude/skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/744) (37 reactions), [#693 — Claude Code cannot read globally installed skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/693) (25), [#403](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/403) (20), [#421](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/421) (18), [#1045](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/1045) (12) — per-harness path correctness is the top failure mode\n- [#283 — skills install/sync from lock file](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/283) (56), [#549 — npm-ci-equivalent restore](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/549) (47), [#11 — RFC: Versioning](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/11) (27) — consumers want deterministic, versioned installs","tokenCount":686}],"storageText":"markdown block\nin docs/research/2026-09-29-user-needs.md\nPurpose: authentication, token management, logging, caching, HTTP/API, file operations\n\n\n**Strongest evidence:** [mcp-remote#316 — Windows OAuth callback listener failure](https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/issues/316), [mcp-cli#24 — Not working on Linux arm64](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/24)\n\n**Difficulty:** for mcp-wire: docs-only (document WSL; jq/curl exist on arm64).\nNative Windows bash port is out of scope per the family's \"bash + npm + GitHub\"\nboundary.\n\n---\n\n## Bucket 2 — DISTRIBUTION / PACKAGING (ranked)\n\n### 1. Zero-runtime, one-line install — \"no node\" is a feature\n**How often:** the most-reacted distribution complaint in the whole MCP space.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [modelcontextprotocol/servers#64 — MCP Servers Don't Work with NVM](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/issues/64) (182 reactions) — node-version hell is the #1 pain of the npx-stdio ecosystem\n- [inspector#326 — `mcp-inspector: command not found` after upgrade](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/issues/326) (20) and [#873 — phantom dependencies](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/issues/873) (12)\n- Distribution evidence: [turlockmike/murl](https://github.com/turlockmike/murl) ships a Homebrew tap; mcpx ships binary + npm + curl script; [evantahler post](https://www.evantahler.com/blog/post/2026-03-13-curl-for-mcp) — \"agents already know curl, git, docker, npm\"\n\n**Difficulty:** low. mcp-wire already has the two winning artifacts (single-file\ncurl install; npm two-tier package). Add a Homebrew tap + keep the engine\ndependency-free (bash/curl/jq only). This is the moat vs. node-based mcpc.\n\n### 2. Agent-harness / skills-ecosystem compatibility\n**How often:** vercel-labs/skills issue tracker is dominated by it — install\npaths, symlinks, lockfiles, versioning.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [vercel-labs/skills#744 — `npx skills add` doesn't create symlinks in ~/.claude/skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/744) (37 reactions), [#693 — Claude Code cannot read globally installed skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/693) (25), [#403](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/403) (20), [#421](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/421) (18), [#1045](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/1045) (12) — per-harness path correctness is the top failure mode\n- [#283 — skills install/sync from lock file](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/283) (56), [#549 — npm-ci-equivalent restore](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/549) (47), [#11 — RFC: Versioning](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/11) (27) — consumers want deterministic, versioned installs","content":"\n**Strongest evidence:** [mcp-remote#316 — Windows OAuth callback listener failure](https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/issues/316), [mcp-cli#24 — Not working on Linux arm64](https://github.com/philschmid/mcp-cli/issues/24)\n\n**Difficulty:** for mcp-wire: docs-only (document WSL; jq/curl exist on arm64).\nNative Windows bash port is out of scope per the family's \"bash + npm + GitHub\"\nboundary.\n\n---\n\n## Bucket 2 — DISTRIBUTION / PACKAGING (ranked)\n\n### 1. Zero-runtime, one-line install — \"no node\" is a feature\n**How often:** the most-reacted distribution complaint in the whole MCP space.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [modelcontextprotocol/servers#64 — MCP Servers Don't Work with NVM](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/issues/64) (182 reactions) — node-version hell is the #1 pain of the npx-stdio ecosystem\n- [inspector#326 — `mcp-inspector: command not found` after upgrade](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/issues/326) (20) and [#873 — phantom dependencies](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/issues/873) (12)\n- Distribution evidence: [turlockmike/murl](https://github.com/turlockmike/murl) ships a Homebrew tap; mcpx ships binary + npm + curl script; [evantahler post](https://www.evantahler.com/blog/post/2026-03-13-curl-for-mcp) — \"agents already know curl, git, docker, npm\"\n\n**Difficulty:** low. mcp-wire already has the two winning artifacts (single-file\ncurl install; npm two-tier package). Add a Homebrew tap + keep the engine\ndependency-free (bash/curl/jq only). This is the moat vs. node-based mcpc.\n\n### 2. Agent-harness / skills-ecosystem compatibility\n**How often:** vercel-labs/skills issue tracker is dominated by it — install\npaths, symlinks, lockfiles, versioning.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [vercel-labs/skills#744 — `npx skills add` doesn't create symlinks in ~/.claude/skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/744) (37 reactions), [#693 — Claude Code cannot read globally installed skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/693) (25), [#403](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/403) (20), [#421](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/421) (18), [#1045](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/1045) (12) — per-harness path correctness is the top failure mode\n- [#283 — skills install/sync from lock file](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/283) (56), [#549 — npm-ci-equivalent restore](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/549) (47), [#11 — RFC: Versioning](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/11) (27) — consumers want deterministic, versioned installs","contentHash":"7192b2653ff0a145","metadata":{"filePath":"docs/research/2026-09-29-user-needs.md","startLine":163,"endLine":192,"chunkType":"block","language":"markdown","hash":"7192b2653ff0a145"}}],"error":"Google embedding provider returned HTTP 400.","attemptCount":11,"lastAttempt":"2026-10-17T11:40:23.914Z"}
{"version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"chunk_5436622696d42090","texts":[{"text":"markdown block\nin docs/research/2026-09-29-user-needs.md\nPurpose: validation, caching, HTTP/API, file operations, data parsing, testing\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [vercel-labs/skills#744 — `npx skills add` doesn't create symlinks in ~/.claude/skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/744) (37 reactions), [#693 — Claude Code cannot read globally installed skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/693) (25), [#403](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/403) (20), [#421](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/421) (18), [#1045](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/1045) (12) — per-harness path correctness is the top failure mode\n- [#283 — skills install/sync from lock file](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/283) (56), [#549 — npm-ci-equivalent restore](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/549) (47), [#11 — RFC: Versioning](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/11) (27) — consumers want deterministic, versioned installs\n- [#381 — Official support for private skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/381) (82) — teams want this in private repos\n\n**Difficulty:** low-medium for mcp-wire: verify `npx skills add\nadhamhaithameid/mcp-wire` lands correctly across Claude Code / Cursor / Codex;\nkeep the vendored-engine version stamp auditable (sync scripts already do\nthis); document the family-package ↔ standalone-skill version relationship\n(also flagged on map #5).\n\n### 3. Discovery: directory listings (skills.sh, MCP registry, server cards)\n**How often:** a steady stream of \"please index me\" issues on skills.sh; the\nregistry spec work exists for exactly this.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- skills.sh index requests, e.g. [vercel-labs/skills#2256 — repo resolves via `add` but never shows in the directory](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/2256), [#2289 — reindex after rename](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/2289)\n- [SEP-1649: MCP Server Cards — HTTP discovery via .well-known](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/1649) (19 reactions) — machine-readable discovery is becoming spec\n- [modelcontextprotocol/registry#494 — relax name-based validation](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/494) — registry onboarding friction\n\n**Difficulty:** low — submit mcp-wire/figma-wire to skills.sh, the MCP registry\n(server.json), awesome-mcp lists. Pure PR work.\n\n### 4. Docs that teach agents (and their humans) the pattern\n**How often:** constant subtext in HN/Reddit debates about context cost.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- HN [MCP: An (Accidentally) Universal Plugin System](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44411118): \"The official MCP documentation completely fails at explaining how it works\" — docs gaps push people to whatever has a great README\n- [Saasufy skills](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48789596): shipping curl commands inside skill markdown \"works great… a single markdown file\" — the skill+CLI pattern is validated\n- HN [MCP is dead?](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48332907): CLIs need discoverable help (\"--short-descr\") because context is the scarce resource — SKILL.md quality is the interface","tokenCount":797}],"storageText":"markdown block\nin docs/research/2026-09-29-user-needs.md\nPurpose: validation, caching, HTTP/API, file operations, data parsing, testing\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- [vercel-labs/skills#744 — `npx skills add` doesn't create symlinks in ~/.claude/skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/744) (37 reactions), [#693 — Claude Code cannot read globally installed skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/693) (25), [#403](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/403) (20), [#421](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/421) (18), [#1045](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/1045) (12) — per-harness path correctness is the top failure mode\n- [#283 — skills install/sync from lock file](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/283) (56), [#549 — npm-ci-equivalent restore](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/549) (47), [#11 — RFC: Versioning](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/11) (27) — consumers want deterministic, versioned installs\n- [#381 — Official support for private skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/381) (82) — teams want this in private repos\n\n**Difficulty:** low-medium for mcp-wire: verify `npx skills add\nadhamhaithameid/mcp-wire` lands correctly across Claude Code / Cursor / Codex;\nkeep the vendored-engine version stamp auditable (sync scripts already do\nthis); document the family-package ↔ standalone-skill version relationship\n(also flagged on map #5).\n\n### 3. Discovery: directory listings (skills.sh, MCP registry, server cards)\n**How often:** a steady stream of \"please index me\" issues on skills.sh; the\nregistry spec work exists for exactly this.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- skills.sh index requests, e.g. [vercel-labs/skills#2256 — repo resolves via `add` but never shows in the directory](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/2256), [#2289 — reindex after rename](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/2289)\n- [SEP-1649: MCP Server Cards — HTTP discovery via .well-known](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/1649) (19 reactions) — machine-readable discovery is becoming spec\n- [modelcontextprotocol/registry#494 — relax name-based validation](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/494) — registry onboarding friction\n\n**Difficulty:** low — submit mcp-wire/figma-wire to skills.sh, the MCP registry\n(server.json), awesome-mcp lists. Pure PR work.\n\n### 4. Docs that teach agents (and their humans) the pattern\n**How often:** constant subtext in HN/Reddit debates about context cost.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- HN [MCP: An (Accidentally) Universal Plugin System](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44411118): \"The official MCP documentation completely fails at explaining how it works\" — docs gaps push people to whatever has a great README\n- [Saasufy skills](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48789596): shipping curl commands inside skill markdown \"works great… a single markdown file\" — the skill+CLI pattern is validated\n- HN [MCP is dead?](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48332907): CLIs need discoverable help (\"--short-descr\") because context is the scarce resource — SKILL.md quality is the interface","content":"**Strongest evidence:**\n- [vercel-labs/skills#744 — `npx skills add` doesn't create symlinks in ~/.claude/skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/744) (37 reactions), [#693 — Claude Code cannot read globally installed skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/693) (25), [#403](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/403) (20), [#421](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/421) (18), [#1045](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/1045) (12) — per-harness path correctness is the top failure mode\n- [#283 — skills install/sync from lock file](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/283) (56), [#549 — npm-ci-equivalent restore](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/549) (47), [#11 — RFC: Versioning](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/11) (27) — consumers want deterministic, versioned installs\n- [#381 — Official support for private skills](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/381) (82) — teams want this in private repos\n\n**Difficulty:** low-medium for mcp-wire: verify `npx skills add\nadhamhaithameid/mcp-wire` lands correctly across Claude Code / Cursor / Codex;\nkeep the vendored-engine version stamp auditable (sync scripts already do\nthis); document the family-package ↔ standalone-skill version relationship\n(also flagged on map #5).\n\n### 3. Discovery: directory listings (skills.sh, MCP registry, server cards)\n**How often:** a steady stream of \"please index me\" issues on skills.sh; the\nregistry spec work exists for exactly this.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- skills.sh index requests, e.g. [vercel-labs/skills#2256 — repo resolves via `add` but never shows in the directory](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/2256), [#2289 — reindex after rename](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/issues/2289)\n- [SEP-1649: MCP Server Cards — HTTP discovery via .well-known](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/1649) (19 reactions) — machine-readable discovery is becoming spec\n- [modelcontextprotocol/registry#494 — relax name-based validation](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/494) — registry onboarding friction\n\n**Difficulty:** low — submit mcp-wire/figma-wire to skills.sh, the MCP registry\n(server.json), awesome-mcp lists. Pure PR work.\n\n### 4. Docs that teach agents (and their humans) the pattern\n**How often:** constant subtext in HN/Reddit debates about context cost.\n\n**Strongest evidence:**\n- HN [MCP: An (Accidentally) Universal Plugin System](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44411118): \"The official MCP documentation completely fails at explaining how it works\" — docs gaps push people to whatever has a great README\n- [Saasufy skills](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48789596): shipping curl commands inside skill markdown \"works great… a single markdown file\" — the skill+CLI pattern is validated\n- HN [MCP is dead?](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48332907): CLIs need discoverable help (\"--short-descr\") because context is the scarce resource — SKILL.md quality is the interface","contentHash":"014b4fbb03e9841c","metadata":{"filePath":"docs/research/2026-09-29-user-needs.md","startLine":190,"endLine":219,"chunkType":"block","language":"markdown","hash":"014b4fbb03e9841c"}}],"error":"Google embedding provider returned HTTP 400.","attemptCount":11,"lastAttempt":"2026-10-17T11:40:23.914Z"}
